    <string name="algo_unknown">Unknown</string>
    <string name="algo_peak_magnitude_name">Peak detection</string>
    <string name="algo_peak_magnitude_short">Peaks</string>
    <string name="algo_peak_magnitude_desc">Counts local maxima of the band-passed acceleration magnitude. A peak is a step when it is at least the minimum interval away from the previous one and its prominence exceeds max(floor, factor × std). Simple, fast baseline; sensitive to shaking and phone handling.</string>
    <string name="algo_adaptive_peak_valley_name">Adaptive peak–valley</string>
    <string name="algo_adaptive_peak_valley_short">Peak–valley</string>
    <string name="algo_adaptive_peak_valley_desc">A step is a peak paired with its nearest valley. The pair counts when the peak–valley difference exceeds an adaptive threshold derived from the local standard deviation, so the detector follows amplitude changes along the walk.</string>
    <string name="algo_zero_crossing_name">Zero crossing</string>
    <string name="algo_zero_crossing_short">Zero cross</string>
    <string name="algo_zero_crossing_desc">Counts positive-going zero crossings of the centred signal, each validated by a following peak above a threshold within a short look-ahead window. Very cheap; depends on good centring and filtering.</string>
    <string name="algo_autocorrelation_name">Autocorrelation cadence</string>
    <string name="algo_autocorrelation_short">Autocorr.</string>
    <string name="algo_autocorrelation_desc">Estimates the gait period in sliding windows from the strongest autocorrelation peak inside the step band, then converts cadence × time into steps. Robust for steady walking; it searches above f_min to avoid locking onto the stride (two steps).</string>
    <string name="algo_fft_cadence_name">FFT cadence</string>
    <string name="algo_fft_cadence_short">FFT</string>
    <string name="algo_fft_cadence_desc">Finds the dominant frequency of each Hann-windowed segment in the step band and sums cadence × time. A stride guard doubles a dominant sub-harmonic when its energy clearly beats the step band.</string>
    <string name="algo_dynamic_threshold_name">Dynamic threshold</string>
    <string name="algo_dynamic_threshold_short">Dyn. thresh.</string>
    <string name="algo_dynamic_threshold_desc">The classic hardware pedometer (Zhao, 2010): the smoothed signal is cut into short windows, the threshold is the midpoint of each window’s max and min, and a step is a downward crossing of that threshold, provided the swing exceeds the minimum amplitude.</string>
    <string name="algo_pan_tompkins_name">Pan–Tompkins energy</string>
    <string name="algo_pan_tompkins_short">Pan–Tompkins</string>
    <string name="algo_pan_tompkins_desc">Borrowed from ECG beat detection: own band-pass → derivative → rectify → square → moving integration → square root. Candidates are accepted against an adaptive threshold between running signal-peak and noise-peak levels.</string>
    <string name="algo_hysteresis_name">Schmitt trigger</string>
    <string name="algo_hysteresis_short">Hysteresis</string>
    <string name="algo_hysteresis_desc">A two-state machine: it arms when the filtered signal drops below −T and fires one step when it rises above +T, with T = max(floor, factor × local std). The hysteresis ignores small wiggles around zero.</string>
    <string name="algo_gyro_peak_name">Gyroscope peaks</string>
    <string name="algo_gyro_peak_short">Gyro</string>
    <string name="algo_gyro_peak_desc">Peak detection on the band-passed gyroscope magnitude. Useful when the phone swings in the hand or rotates with the hip; depending on placement it may count strides or extra swings, which makes it a good contrast to the accelerometer methods.</string>
    <string name="algo_vertical_accel_name">Vertical acceleration</string>
    <string name="algo_vertical_accel_short">Vertical</string>
    <string name="algo_vertical_accel_desc">Gravity is estimated with a slow low-pass filter on the raw accelerometer vector and the acceleration is projected onto that direction. The resulting sign-consistent vertical signal is band-passed and peak-detected; it ignores horizontal sway.</string>
