    <string name="settings_about">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_text">Everything stays on the device: sensor files, GPS tracks and the SQLite database live in the app’s private folder. Icons by Lucide.</string>
    <string name="info_title">How the algorithms work</string>
    <string name="info_subtitle">Pipeline, algorithms, step-length models and confidence</string>
    <string name="info_pipeline_title">Pipeline</string>
    <string name="info_pipeline_text">Raw samples are resampled onto a common grid (default 100 Hz). The accelerometer magnitude |a| is orientation independent; its median (gravity) is removed and a zero-phase Butterworth band-pass (default 0.5–4 Hz) keeps the walking frequencies. Every algorithm then works on this filtered signal (or on the gyroscope / vertical component). Confidence combines interval regularity, global periodicity, amplitude consistency and GPS plausibility; the highest-scoring algorithm is recommended.</string>
    <string name="info_algorithms_section">Step counting algorithms</string>
    <string name="info_methods_section">Step length methods</string>
    <string name="info_confidence_title">Confidence score</string>
    <string name="info_confidence_text">Without GPS: 0.42 × interval regularity + 0.33 × periodicity + 0.25 × amplitude consistency. With GPS: 0.30 × intervals + 0.22 × periodicity + 0.28 × GPS plausibility (implied step length 0.45–0.95 m is ideal, 0.25–2.2 m plausible) + 0.20 × amplitude. Frequency methods use the global periodicity in place of per-step measures.</string>
